6739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "6\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126739" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\,i+6\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩$ at the point where $t=\\pi ,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the point where $t=\\pi ,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(\\pi )+u{r}^{′}(\\pi ),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(\\pi ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨0,1⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0556f4231178acbf98d5a5a68ef76c593c42aaaedf71e8d6a11c56d7a7fe16db" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨-1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨-1,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,0⟩+u⟨0,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,1⟩+u⟨-1,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-126838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,1⟩+u⟨0,1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+{sin}^{2}t\\,k$ at the point corresponding to $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "At the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$,  the vector ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+u{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(\\frac{\\pi }{4}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j+{sin}^{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,k \\\\  & =\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({sin}^{2}t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,i+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\,j-\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})k \\\\  & =\\,i-\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point \n where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(\\,i-\\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0556f4231178acbf98d5a5a68ef76c593c42aaaedf71e8d6a11c56d7a7fe16db" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(-\\,i+2\\,j+\\,k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(2\\,i-\\,j+\\,k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(\\,i+2\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(\\,i-\\,j+\\,k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33461" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\,i+\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k+u(i-\\,j+\\frac{1}{2}\\,k)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+(1+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,j$, find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =i+t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ [t\\,i+(1+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,j]\\cdot (i+t\\,j) & =0 \\\\ t\\cdot 1+(1+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\cdot t & =0 \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{3} & =0 \\\\ t(4+{t}^{2}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only solution is $t=0$ since $4+{t}^{2}>0$ for any $t.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)=0\\,i+(1+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2})\\,j=j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the point $(0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0556f4231178acbf98d5a5a68ef76c593c42aaaedf71e8d6a11c56d7a7fe16db" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the curve $r(t)=t\\,i+(2+{t}^{3})\\,j+(1+{t}^{2})\\,k$, find all points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+{t}^{3})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =i+\\,3{t}^{2}\\,j+\\,2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that $r({t}_{0})=c\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =c\\,{r}^{′}(t) \\\\ t\\,i+(2+{t}^{3})\\,j+(1+{t}^{2})\\,k & =c(i+\\,3{t}^{2}\\,j+\\,2t\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ gives:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}t=c \\\\ 2+{t}^{3}=c(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ 1+{t}^{2}=c(2t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation we obtain $t=c.$ Substituting $c=t$ into the second equality gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+{t}^{3} & =3{t}^{3} \\\\ 2 & =2{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & =1 \\\\ t & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis satisfies also the equation $1+{t}^{2}=c(2t).$\nTherefore, $r$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the point corresponding to $t=1.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(1) & =i+(2+{1}^{3})\\,j+(1+{1}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =i+3\\,j+2\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the point $P(1,3,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33509" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0556f4231178acbf98d5a5a68ef76c593c42aaaedf71e8d6a11c56d7a7fe16db" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33509" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "(0,2,1)"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/state.json" "file_sha256" "650416bffcabe436ad78a349440d52b26e024954aa80b568c20859a03b60249d" "basis" 1724 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049728/edb-import/verification.json"} {